{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"1f19acb3bece9d73","name":"card_unit_t_28_pincer","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Breakthrough/units/card_unit_t_28_pincer","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"T-28","text":"Pincer: When this unit is destroyed, put it on top of owner's deck.","flavorText":"The T-28 was a Soviet medium tank that was introduced in the early 1930s and used by the Soviet Union and other forces prior to and during WWII. The tank was intended for infantry support and many of them were deployed by the Red Army during the Winter War with Finland and the Soviet Invasion of Poland. At the start of Operation Barbarossa the Red Army had 411 T-28 tanks available, but most of them were lost during the first months of the invasion, either in combat or they were abandoned after mechanical breakdown. The T-28 had a crew of six, a main armament of a 76.2 mm KT-28 howitzer and secondary armament of 4-5 x 7.62 mm DT machine guns. A total of 503 tanks were produced, including variants, but very few were still in use after 1941.","faction":"Soviet","type":"tank","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_t_28_pincer","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_t_28_pincer_title","SourceString":"T-28","LocalizedString":"T-28"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::tank","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_t_28_pincer_text","SourceString":"Pincer: When this unit is destroyed, put it on top of owner's deck.","LocalizedString":"Pincer: When this unit is destroyed, put it on top of owner's deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_t_28_pincer_history","SourceString":"The T-28 was a Soviet medium tank that was introduced in the early 1930s and used by the Soviet Union and other forces prior to and during WWII. The tank was intended for infantry support and many of them were deployed by the Red Army during the Winter War with Finland and the Soviet Invasion of Poland. At the start of Operation Barbarossa the Red Army had 411 T-28 tanks available, but most of them were lost during the first months of the invasion, either in combat or they were abandoned after mechanical breakdown. The T-28 had a crew of six, a main armament of a 76.2 mm KT-28 howitzer and secondary armament of 4-5 x 7.62 mm DT machine guns. A total of 503 tanks were produced, including variants, but very few were still in use after 1941.","LocalizedString":"The T-28 was a Soviet medium tank that was introduced in the early 1930s and used by the Soviet Union and other forces prior to and during WWII. The tank was intended for infantry support and many of them were deployed by the Red Army during the Winter War with Finland and the Soviet Invasion of Poland. At the start of Operation Barbarossa the Red Army had 411 T-28 tanks available, but most of them were lost during the first months of the invasion, either in combat or they were abandoned after mechanical breakdown. The T-28 had a crew of six, a main armament of a 76.2 mm KT-28 howitzer and secondary armament of 4-5 x 7.62 mm DT machine guns. A total of 503 tanks were produced, including variants, but very few were still in use after 1941."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardLeaveBoardOrOwner","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSuppressed","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardDestroyed"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Pincer"],"hasBlitz":true,"hasSmokescreen":true,"hasPincer":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Tank_Medium_Move_Fx'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Tank_Medium_Move_Fx.0"},"soundMoveToFrontline":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Tank_Medium_Move_Fx'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audi